                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Its cute and cheap, but awkward and I'm not sure how enjoyable it really is...\n\nInteractions are awkward: \n\n1.) Having a mouse cursor which is moved by arrows really takes you out of the platforming experience and slows everything down!\n\n2.) It would have been better with diagonal firing, since the enemies can!  It has the feel of a dated platformer, NOT in a good way.\n\n3.) There are things that are are counter intuitive, such as the fractions of resources are inversed!  Basic math here, which makes the game not only look bad, but the player has to think backwards. \n\nIt is actually a bit tedious and boring with little challenge.  I find myself getting hit only out of laziness, since you can sit back at range most of the time.\n\nI am just not compelled to complete the game (160 levels), with so many other more enjoyable titles in my library and on Steam.\n\n\n\nDISCLAIMER:  These are my opinions about the experience I had playing this game.  I share them in hopes that people who are like minded will either enjoy a suggested game, or avoid frustration wasting time and money on something I felt was a personal waste.  Please feel free to comment positively, but know that anything that trolls or is just simply negative comments will be quickly deleted.  The reality is, that my reviews are for people who do not own the game, not to initiate philosophical dialogue about it.  If you are passionate about this game, please feel free to share that in your own review.",
